  "_about": "How each material reflects light. roughness: 0 = mirror, 1 = fully matte (GGX, Disney remap). f0: reflectance straight on; ~0.04 for paint, plastic, varnish, glass (index 1.5); 0.02-0.03 for fibres. metal: 1 = metal (reflection tinted by the texture). bump: relief depth in inches (bump shading and parallax), from a height field built from the texture's fine detail. Only for real geometry in the texture (grout, ceiling-tile grid, carpet pile): on printed or painted surfaces it turns pixels into lumps, so 0. relief: size in inches of the detail read as relief (pile ~0.25, grout ~1). gloss: how much of the specular reflection shows (0 = matte, as paint and carpet look in the references). sheen: fibre sheen at grazing angles. cavity: darkening of the deepest crevices. 'textures' overrides a single texture by name.",
